{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_connect_widget", "label": "Embedded Eko Connect widget (<tf-wlc-widget>)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_token_endpoint", "label": "GET /connect/token endpoint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The widget reads sessionStorage in the host realm and has no token prop or postMessage API, while this app's session is an HttpOnly cookie \u2014 so supporting it required deliberately publishing an upstream credential to the browser. /connect/* is mounted only when CONNECT_API_BASE_URL is set."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_access_token_lite", "label": "access_token_lite exposure trade-off", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Setting the lite token means the widget's full-token fallback never fires, so the full access token and refresh token stay server-side; the two exposed tokens are XSS-readable only while a flow is on screen and are cleared on unmount, sign-out and expiry."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_token_before_runtime", "label": "Tokens written before the runtime loads", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The widget starts calling connect-api the moment it upgrades; a request that beats the token into storage goes out as Bearer null."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_support_ticket", "label": "Server-side support-ticket assembly", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zoho-Desk formatting lives server-side so the console never learns the ticket schema and cannot claim to be a different user; caps on attachments, fields and free text are enforced at the trust boundary, the browser check being only a courtesy."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_dialog_provider", "label": "ConnectDialogProvider (promise-per-dialog stack)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces Eloka's 571-line pub/sub loader, whose indirection existed only because it was mounted in a Next.js layout that could not see its callers; every dialog is React.lazy so webcam/crop/MediaPipe stay out of the initial bundle."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_fileupload", "label": "<FileUpload> control", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every image routes through the editor before the caller sees it, so a form receives a cropped, size-capped JPEG instead of a 4 MB photo of a desk."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_watermark", "label": "Watermark provenance stamping", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A KYC photo is evidence and evidence without provenance can be re-used for another customer; coordinates can be spoofed on a rooted phone while an observed IP cannot, so the line carries both, resolved on mount so a late prompt cannot stamp a blank location."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_syncwidgetprops", "label": "syncWidgetProps (React 19 property gotcha)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "React 19 assigns properties on an upgraded custom element where older React set attributes, and Polymer only JSON-parses attributes \u2014 so real objects are assigned via a ref, with interaction_id last because it is the observed property that starts the flow."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_id_vs_type_id", "label": "id vs interaction_type_id", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "interaction_type_id is 0 for every composite interaction, so keying role_trxn_list by type collapses them all onto \"0\" and entitlement lookup finds nothing; rows are passed through whole because the widget reads behavior, group_interaction_ids, icon and uri too."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_cors_blocker", "label": "connect-api CORS allowlist blocker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every widget request is cross-origin and cannot be fixed from this repo, so VITE_SHOW_CONNECT_WIDGET stays false until connect-api allowlists the console origin."}, {"id": "docs_features_connect_widget_dev_bench", "label": "/console/test DEV dialog bench", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dialogs are hard to reach through a real flow, so a DEV-only bench opens each directly; route and rail item sit behind import.meta.env.DEV with the import inside the guard so no chunk ships in production."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_console_roadmap_developer_console", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_connect_widget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_console_roadmap_walletbalance", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_connect_widget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_developer_docs_try_it_now_dev_only_creds", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_dev_bench", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_features_connect_widget_connect_widget", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_token_endpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_features_connect_widget_token_endpoint", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_access_token_lite", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_features_connect_widget_connect_widget", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_token_before_runtime", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_features_connect_widget_connect_widget", "target": "docs_features_connect_widget_syncwidgetprops", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/features/connect-widget.md", "source_location": nul